# PART 23 — DEVELOPMENT RULES FOR ANDROID STUDIO AI ASSISTANT

These instructions are mandatory throughout development.

## Rule 1 — Read Before Editing

Before changing any existing file:

- Inspect the existing project.
- Understand the current architecture.
- Identify dependencies.
- Review related classes.
- Check existing tests.
- Understand the impact of the change.

Never blindly overwrite existing files.

## Rule 2 — Build Incrementally

Do not generate the entire application in one enormous unverified code dump.

Implement one logical module at a time.

Build after every major implementation stage.

## Rule 3 — Preserve Existing Functionality

When implementing new features:

- Do not remove existing working functionality.
- Do not rename public classes unnecessarily.
- Do not replace working architecture without a documented reason.
- Do not remove database migrations.
- Do not reset the database during ordinary updates.
- Do not introduce duplicate implementations.

## Rule 4 — No Fake Functionality

Never create buttons that appear functional but do nothing.

Never use hardcoded fake statistics in the actual application.

Never simulate successful backup or restore.

Never display fabricated progress.

If a feature is not implemented, mark it clearly as Pending or Not Yet Available.

## Rule 5 — Compile and Verify

After each major module:

1. Sync Gradle.
2. Compile.
3. Run Unit Tests.
4. Run Relevant UI Tests.
5. Inspect Build Output.
6. Fix Errors.
7. Verify Existing Features.
8. Report Results.

## Rule 6 — Database Safety

Any schema modification requires a proper Room Migration.

Never use destructive database migration in production.

Never discard user data to solve a migration issue.

## Rule 7 — Progress Accuracy

Progress calculation must be implemented in the Domain Layer.

All calculations must have Unit Tests.

No inconsistent Progress values are allowed.

## Rule 8 — Documentation

Maintain:

- README.md.
- ARCHITECTURE.md.
- DATABASE_SCHEMA.md.
- DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md.
- CHANGELOG.md.
- TESTING.md.

Update relevant documentation after every completed phase.

## Rule 9 — Code Quality

- No unnecessary code duplication.
- No unexplained magic numbers.
- No unused dependencies.
- No unresolved TODOs in completed modules.
- No ignored critical exceptions.
- No hardcoded secrets.
- No unnecessary network permissions.

## Rule 10 — Honest Reporting

At the end of each development task, report:

- Files Created.
- Files Modified.
- Features Completed.
- Build Status.
- Tests Passed.
- Tests Failed.
- Known Issues.
- Next Recommended Step.

Never claim successful implementation without verification.

